The intercom hisses, then the voice comes back, closer to the speaker now. "Just me. I'm in the cold locker, and the door has decided it likes me." A pause. Something heavy shifts behind the words. "Also, I was told you'd be the one who knows where Ilse's compass went."

The compass sits warm in your palm.

