You leave the lentils and take the aft corridor. The cold locker door is steel, rimed white at the seam, and the handle will not move. Frost has crept along the hinge. From inside, a knuckle raps twice. Then the voice, muffled and patient: "That compass. Does it still point at anything?"

The needle in your pocket has shifted its aim.

*If you want to force the locker before whoever is inside answers for himself, that would be a Face Danger.*

